<article class="env-definition" id="08TJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08TJ">Definition <span data-tag="08TJ">17.31.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $\mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings. The <em>naive cotangent complex</em> $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{\mathcal{B}/\mathcal{A}}$ is the chain complex (<a href="/tag/08TI" data-tag="08TI">17.31.0.2</a>) </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{\mathcal{B}/\mathcal{A}} = \left(\mathcal{I}/\mathcal{I}^2 \longrightarrow \Omega _{\mathcal{A}[\mathcal{B}]/\mathcal{A}} \otimes _{\mathcal{A}[\mathcal{B}]} \mathcal{B}\right)  \]
</div>
  <p> with $\mathcal{I}/\mathcal{I}^2$ placed in degree $-1$ and $\Omega _{\mathcal{A}[\mathcal{B}]/\mathcal{A}} \otimes _{\mathcal{A}[\mathcal{B}]} \mathcal{B}$ placed in degree $0$. </p>
</article>